invariant: INV-39
file: tcp_nonblocking_step.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-nonblocking client installs the handshake keys with bytes
  still unread after the ServerHello in its record, and reads them as the
  next message under keys that never protected them. RFC 9846 section 5.1
  makes that unexpected_message. test/tcp_nonblocking_record_end_tests.h
  adds one byte to the ServerHello's record and requires that alert.

--- old
    // The read key changes after the ServerHello, so the ServerHello must
    // end its record (hsr_check_record_end).
    rc = hsr_check_record_end(&r->hs);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
--- new
